# Deployment Procedures

## Quick Commands

### PM2 Server Management (Development)
```bash
# Start AI agent server (background PM2 process)
npm run ai:start

# Health check
npm run ai:health

# Check server status and port
npm run ai:status
npm run ai:port

# View logs (last 100 lines)
npm run ai:logs

# Restart server
npm run ai:restart

# Stop server
npm run ai:stop

# Verify port availability
npm run ai:verify-port
```

### Fly.io Quick Deployment Checklist
```bash
# 1. Install & login
brew install flyctl
fly auth login

# 2. Create app
fly apps create ai-calendar-helper --org personal --region sea

# 3. Provision & Attach DB
fly postgres create --name ai-calendar-helper-db --region sea --initial-cluster-size 1 --volume-size 1
fly postgres attach --app ai-calendar-helper ai-calendar-helper-db

# 4. Import Secrets from a local .env.production file
fly secrets import < .env.production --app ai-calendar-helper

# 5. Deploy (using remote builder)
npm run deploy:fly

# 6. Health check
curl -f https://ai-calendar-helper.fly.dev/api/health
```

### Build & Validation
```bash
# Full build validation before deploy
npm run build:clean

# Run complete test suite
npm run test:ci

# Check for linting issues
npm run validate

# Bundle analysis
npm run build:analyze

# Scale application
fly scale count 2 --app ai-calendar-helper
```

## PM2 Configuration

### Local Development Server (`ecosystem.config.js`)
```javascript
module.exports = {
  apps: [{
    name: 'ai-calendar-helper',
    script: 'node_modules/.bin/next',
    args: 'start -p 3777',
    cwd: '/Users/cam/Documents/Projects/ai-calendar-helper',
    env: {
      NODE_ENV: 'production',
      PORT: '3777',
    },
    instances: 1,
    exec_mode: 'fork',
    watch: false,
    max_memory_restart: '1G',
    error_file: './logs/err.log',
    out_file: './logs/out.log',
    log_file: './logs/combined.log',
    time: true
  }]
};
```

### PM2 Troubleshooting
**Server won't start**:
```bash
# Check PM2 process list
pm2 list

# Delete stuck processes
pm2 delete ai-calendar-helper

# Start with verbose logging
PM2_DEBUG=true npm run ai:start

# Check port conflicts
lsof -i :3777
```

**Memory issues**:
```bash
# Monitor resource usage
pm2 monit

# Check memory restart events
pm2 logs --lines 50

# Restart with increased memory
pm2 restart ai-calendar-helper --max-memory-restart 2G
```

## Fly.io Configuration

### App Configuration (`fly.toml`)
```toml
app = "ai-calendar-helper"
primary_region = "sea"

[build]
  builder = "heroku/buildpacks:20"

[env]
  NODE_ENV = "production"
  PORT = "8080"

[http_service]
  internal_port = 8080
  force_https = true
  auto_stop_machines = true
  auto_start_machines = true
  min_machines_running = 0

[[statics]]
  guest_path = "/app/public"
  url_prefix = "/static/"
```

### Environment Variables Management
```bash
# Set production environment variables
fly secrets set NEXTAUTH_SECRET="$(openssl rand -base64 32)" --app ai-calendar-helper
fly secrets set DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..." --app ai-calendar-helper
fly secrets set GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID="..." --app ai-calendar-helper
fly secrets set GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET="..." --app ai-calendar-helper
fly secrets set OPENAI_API_KEY="..." --app ai-calendar-helper

# List current secrets
fly secrets list --app ai-calendar-helper

# Remove a secret
fly secrets unset SECRET_NAME --app ai-calendar-helper
```

### Database Management
```bash
# Create Postgres database
fly postgres create --name ai-calendar-helper-db --region sea

# Get database URL
fly postgres connect --app ai-calendar-helper-db

# Run migrations on production
fly ssh console --app ai-calendar-helper
npx prisma migrate deploy
```

## Deployment Workflows

### Pre-deployment Checklist
- [ ] All tests passing: `npm run test:ci`
- [ ] No linting errors: `npm run validate`
- [ ] Environment variables set in Fly.io
- [ ] Database migrations ready
- [ ] Production build successful: `npm run build`

### Standard Deployment Process
```bash
# 1. Validate locally
npm run validate && npm test && npm run test:e2e

# 2. Build production bundle
npm run build

# 3. Deploy to Fly.io
npm run deploy:fly

# 4. Verify deployment
fly status --app ai-calendar-helper
curl -I https://ai-calendar-helper.fly.dev/api/health

# 5. Check application logs
fly logs --app ai-calendar-helper
```

### Emergency Rollback
```bash
# List recent releases
fly releases --app ai-calendar-helper

# Rollback to previous version
fly releases rollback v2 --app ai-calendar-helper

# Check rollback status
fly status --app ai-calendar-helper
```

## Production Troubleshooting

### Application Not Starting
**Check deployment logs**:
```bash
fly logs --app ai-calendar-helper | tail -50
```

**Common issues**:
1. Missing environment variables → Check `fly secrets list`
2. Database connection → Verify `DATABASE_URL` secret
3. Build failures → Check `fly logs` during deployment
4. Port binding → Ensure app listens on `$PORT` or 8080

### Performance Issues
**Monitor resource usage**:
```bash
fly status --app ai-calendar-helper
fly logs --app ai-calendar-helper | grep -E "(memory|cpu)"
```

**Scale resources**:
```bash
# Increase machine size
fly scale vm shared-cpu-2x --app ai-calendar-helper

# Add more instances
fly scale count 2 --app ai-calendar-helper
```

### Database Connection Issues
**Check connection**:
```bash
fly ssh console --app ai-calendar-helper
node -e "require('./lib/prisma').prisma.\$queryRaw\`SELECT 1\`.then(console.log)"
```

**Reset connections**:
```bash
# Restart application
fly apps restart ai-calendar-helper

# Check database status
fly postgres list
```

### SSL/HTTPS Issues
**Force HTTPS redirect** (already configured in fly.toml):
```toml
[http_service]
  force_https = true
```

**Certificate problems**:
```bash
# Check certificate status
fly certs list --app ai-calendar-helper

# Add custom domain certificate
fly certs create yourdomain.com --app ai-calendar-helper
```

